  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c6e2c649-e4af-5acb-9b5d-98eb64803e10" activityNameId="78ac7ee7-c24d-5f88-bcb1-84247d3fa295" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Biogas, from slurry, at agricultural co-fermentation, covered</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Biogas, from slurry, at agricultural co-fermentation, covered
The inventory refers to a typical agricultural biogas plant in the year 2006 with a capacity of 500m3 and a life time of 20 years.;
UUID: 5abcdc6e-68af-3722-b33e-bbff95724ca5
The process includes the energy use and the infrastructure used to produce 1 Nm3 of biogas from manure in a plant with a covered stock to recover the methane emissions
Location: This process refers to an agricultural biogas plant with a capacity of about 500m3. The data were sampled from 20 different plants in Switzerland. 
Technology: To avoid Methane emissions the new plants in Switzerland are covered, to reduce NH3 emissions the digested matter will be spread with a trail hose.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 12 mio. m3 Biogas 
Sampling: The data are the average of 20 plants in Switzerland to produce electricity according the criteria of "Naturemade" 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5abcdc6e-68af-3722-b33e-bbff95724ca5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
